  "text": "Then we compared methods. Ordinary regression gives an understandable baseline. Adjusted intervals examine correlated errors. A robust slope checks unusual years. We tested the candidates on 20,000 synthetic records. Under strong dependence, none of the deployable candidates passed every screening case. So we kept the alternatives visible, documented their failures, and avoided presenting one interval as a universal fix. This is exploration, not forecasting."
